<section class="solution-section">
  <div class="section-label">The Solution</div>
  <h2>You don't need a smarter model.</h2>
  <h2 class="accent">You need a smarter process.</h2>

  <p class="section-desc">
    Parliament puts multiple AI agents with different cognitive postures in a room to 
    debate a topic on a shared blackboard. They argue, they challenge, they synthesize — 
    until they reach consensus, surface an irreconcilable split, or hit a timeout.
  </p>

  <div class="features">
    <div class="feature">
      <h3>Neurotypes</h3>
      <p>Thirteen specialized deliberation postures — Proposer, Skeptic, Empiricist, Historian, Forecaster, Pragmatist, Lateralist, and more. Each brings a different lens to the same problem.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <h3>Topology Presets</h3>
      <p>Compose neurotypes into reusable deliberation shapes. <code>jury</code> for avoiding framing bias. <code>long-view</code> for long-term consequences. <code>reframe</code> for stuck thinking.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <h3>Echo Detection</h3>
      <p>The Sentry monitors for agreement loops. The Opinion Shift Index tracks whether agents are actually moving or just repeating themselves. Premature consensus gets disrupted by the Red Agent.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <h3>Local-First</h3>
      <p>Runs on oMLX with local models. Privacy-preserving, no API keys needed. Multi-provider support for Ollama, LM Studio, and OpenAI-compatible backends.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <blockquote class="quote">
    <p>"Parliament isn't about chaining agents. It's about putting them in a room and letting them disagree productively."</p>
  </blockquote>
</section>

<style>
